1
00:00:21,239 --> 00:00:21,839
Fu Yan,

2
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,000
do you take Su Juan to be your wife,

3
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,559
from this day forward,

4
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:29,399
for richer, for poorer,

5
00:00:30,039 --> 00:00:32,079
in sickness and in health,

6
00:00:32,520 --> 00:00:34,560
for better, for worse,

7
00:00:35,560 --> 00:00:39,439
to love, honor, and protect her,

8
00:00:39,840 --> 00:00:41,600
as long as you both shall live?

9
00:00:42,159 --> 00:00:44,640
Do you?

10
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:46,759
I do.

11
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:25,640
Watch it!

12
00:01:25,719 --> 00:01:27,159
Watch where you're going!

13
00:01:27,439 --> 00:01:28,640
Got a death wish?

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,439
Why didn't you save me?

15
00:02:20,840 --> 00:02:21,479
You...

16
00:02:24,159 --> 00:02:25,560
You're beyond saving.

17
00:02:25,639 --> 00:02:26,680
Nonsense.

18
00:02:27,479 --> 00:02:29,159
I'm alive and well, aren't I?

19
00:02:30,400 --> 00:02:32,039
Take a good look at yourself.

20
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:13,159
You're already

21
00:03:16,439 --> 00:03:17,319
dead.

22
00:03:26,439 --> 00:03:27,919
Did this just happen?

23
00:03:30,599 --> 00:03:31,400
No.

24
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:38,080
It was seven years ago.

25
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:50,879
What do you think?

26
00:03:51,599 --> 00:03:52,680
It looks amazing.

27
00:03:53,439 --> 00:03:54,960
But I feel like

28
00:03:55,319 --> 00:03:56,719
this part is a bit...

29
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:57,719
No.

30
00:03:57,719 --> 00:03:58,879
Not at all.

31
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,280
It looks amazing.

32
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:19,040
I quite like this one too.

33
00:04:19,879 --> 00:04:22,199
Why didn't your husband come with you?

34
00:04:24,399 --> 00:04:25,759
I want to surprise him.

35
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:36,519
My phone, thanks.

36
00:04:37,959 --> 00:04:38,800
It's my husband.

37
00:04:42,279 --> 00:04:42,839
Hello?

38
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:54,639
Hello.

39
00:04:55,079 --> 00:04:56,720
We can't unlock this guy's phone.

40
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:58,680
We saw an emergency contact saved on it,

41
00:04:58,680 --> 00:04:59,480
so we called.

42
00:04:59,480 --> 00:05:00,879
He was in a car accident.

43
00:05:00,879 --> 00:05:02,120
You need to get here right away.

44
00:05:14,519 --> 00:05:15,839
It's been seven years.

45
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:18,600
Ever since then,

46
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,720
you've been trapped at 25.

47
00:05:26,399 --> 00:05:27,720
Why didn't you tell me?

48
00:05:29,199 --> 00:05:30,399
I tried.

49
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:33,879
I've told you so many times.

50
00:05:35,959 --> 00:05:37,240
But before long,

51
00:05:38,399 --> 00:05:40,079
you'd forget everything,

52
00:05:41,879 --> 00:05:43,480
pretending you were still alive.

53
00:05:45,399 --> 00:05:47,439
Is the person you've been holding onto...

54
00:05:48,279 --> 00:05:50,519
just this version of me?

55
00:05:52,319 --> 00:05:53,439
I can't live without you.

56
00:05:55,519 --> 00:05:56,879
Even if it's just a nightmare,

57
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,600
I'll go through it with you.

58
00:06:21,639 --> 00:06:22,680
Back then,

59
00:06:25,199 --> 00:06:26,360
I wasn't dead.

60
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,879
You're the one who gave up on saving me.

61
00:06:47,399 --> 00:06:48,639
Dad! Mom!

62
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,639
Where's Fu Yan? Where's Fu Yan?

63
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,439
Hello.

64
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,920
I'm the one who called the ambulance.

65
00:06:57,680 --> 00:06:59,600
Oh, right. When he crashed,

66
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:00,839
he was clutching this in his hand.

67
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:15,279
Door opening.

68
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,759
Are you Fu Yan's family?

69
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:20,639
Doctor, how is he?

70
00:07:21,399 --> 00:07:22,920
Things aren't looking good right now.

71
00:07:23,199 --> 00:07:24,560
The patient could die at any moment.

72
00:07:25,199 --> 00:07:26,160
What do you mean?

73
00:07:26,639 --> 00:07:27,399
And you are?

74
00:07:27,519 --> 00:07:28,600
I'm his wife.

75
00:07:29,079 --> 00:07:30,279
The patient has an intracranial hemorrhage.

76
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:31,879
It's compressing the brain tissue.

77
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:34,160
We've stabilized his brain pressure,

78
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:36,000
but the bleeding continues.

79
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,560
Then keep treating him!

80
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,519
We need your consent for this

81
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:41,959
before we can perform a craniotomy.

82
00:07:42,079 --> 00:07:43,160
Are there any risks?

83
00:07:44,079 --> 00:07:45,439
The worst-case scenario

84
00:07:46,160 --> 00:07:47,639
is that he might die.

85
00:07:51,079 --> 00:07:53,279
Is... isn't there any other way?

86
00:07:53,959 --> 00:07:55,399
If we don't operate,

87
00:07:56,079 --> 00:07:57,879
his chances of survival will be even lower.

88
00:07:58,319 --> 00:08:00,399
But there's one thing I must make clear.

89
00:08:00,879 --> 00:08:02,199
Even if the surgery is successful,

90
00:08:02,560 --> 00:08:03,680
the patient will still suffer from

91
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
a severe after-effect.

92
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,199
Which is mobility impairment.

93
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:09,759
I've explained the situation clearly.

94
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:11,959
If you want to proceed with the surgery,

95
00:08:12,759 --> 00:08:14,439
you need to sign the consent form as soon as possible.

96
00:08:15,319 --> 00:08:16,399
Of course we have to save him.

97
00:08:16,959 --> 00:08:18,399
We must save his life at all costs.

98
00:08:18,399 --> 00:08:20,560
Right, you have to save him!

99
00:08:20,879 --> 00:08:23,319
Please take a moment to consider it.

100
00:08:29,079 --> 00:08:30,079
I did save you.

101
00:08:32,399 --> 00:08:34,080
It was the surgery that failed.

102
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:54,919
I believe you.

103
00:08:58,080 --> 00:08:59,200
But this nightmare...

104
00:09:02,919 --> 00:09:04,600
...doesn't need to go on.

105
00:09:44,879 --> 00:09:46,240
Have a seat. This is my stop.

106
00:10:10,559 --> 00:10:12,559
I... I'm almost at my stop.

107
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:14,639
You again.

108
00:10:15,919 --> 00:10:18,679
Yeah, we head to work around the same time.

109
00:10:20,080 --> 00:10:21,320
Where do you work?

110
00:10:23,120 --> 00:10:25,000
I... I work at the Vitality Community.

111
00:10:25,399 --> 00:10:26,200
At the...

112
00:10:26,279 --> 00:10:27,519
I... I'm a screenwriter.

113
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,399
We're at that creative studio.

114
00:10:33,279 --> 00:10:34,159
Sorry about that.

115
00:10:36,519 --> 00:10:37,759
Are you alright, young man?

116
00:10:38,320 --> 00:10:39,720
If you two aren't going to sit, I will.

117
00:10:40,159 --> 00:10:41,159
Please, take a seat.

118
00:10:56,799 --> 00:10:58,120
You like Jacky Cheung too?

119
00:10:59,639 --> 00:11:00,279
Yeah.

120
00:11:00,879 --> 00:11:01,519
Why?

121
00:11:02,279 --> 00:11:03,159
Nothing.

122
00:11:03,879 --> 00:11:05,279
I... I happen to have two

123
00:11:05,279 --> 00:11:06,559
Jacky Cheung concert tickets.

124
00:11:07,080 --> 00:11:08,240
I... I was planning to go with a friend,

125
00:11:10,039 --> 00:11:12,159
a buddy of mine.

126
00:11:12,279 --> 00:11:13,799
But something suddenly came up for him.

127
00:11:14,399 --> 00:11:16,600
So, you like Jacky Cheung too.

128
00:11:16,919 --> 00:11:17,840
What a coincidence.

129
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:18,919
I just wanted to ask you

130
00:11:18,919 --> 00:11:19,759
if you could...

131
00:11:20,399 --> 00:11:22,320
if you'd be willing to go with me.

132
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,600
You don't have to pay me.

133
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:36,639
If you don't go,

134
00:11:37,399 --> 00:11:38,440
the ticket will go to waste.

135
00:11:41,320 --> 00:11:42,759
Shouldn't you send the concert info

136
00:11:42,759 --> 00:11:43,480
to me?

137
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:47,679
Okay.

138
00:12:00,159 --> 00:12:00,759
Thank you.

139
00:12:01,159 --> 00:12:02,159
Young man,

140
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:03,759
you missed your stop.

141
00:12:44,159 --> 00:12:45,159
Hello, President Han.

142
00:12:48,039 --> 00:12:48,879
An exorcism?

143
00:12:53,759 --> 00:12:54,519
Okay.

144
00:12:55,279 --> 00:12:57,000
But why so sudden?

145
00:12:57,639 --> 00:12:59,759
My mom insists she didn't trip on her own.

146
00:13:00,159 --> 00:13:00,840
It was...

147
00:13:01,120 --> 00:13:02,240
it was an unclean thing

148
00:13:02,559 --> 00:13:03,960
that tripped her from under the bed.

149
00:13:05,600 --> 00:13:06,080
Well...

150
00:13:07,679 --> 00:13:08,440
Alright.

151
00:13:09,559 --> 00:13:11,080
I'm heading to a meeting soon.

152
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,120
I'll leave my mom in your hands.

153
00:13:12,360 --> 00:13:13,600
Okay, I got it.

154
00:13:14,679 --> 00:13:15,679
Don't worry.

155
00:13:36,320 --> 00:13:37,120
Master Wu.

156
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:39,039
And you are?

157
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,519
President Han is my boss.

158
00:13:43,759 --> 00:13:44,399
Let's go.

159
00:13:49,879 --> 00:13:51,399
Okay, now close your eyes.

160
00:13:52,159 --> 00:13:53,120
Concentrate.

161
00:14:12,159 --> 00:14:13,080
Feeling a bit better?

162
00:14:23,159 --> 00:14:24,759
Thank you, Master Wu.

163
00:14:25,039 --> 00:14:26,559
I'm glad you came.

164
00:14:27,799 --> 00:14:28,600
Get some rest.

165
00:14:28,919 --> 00:14:30,840
Call me if you need me again.

166
00:14:35,879 --> 00:14:36,679
Come with me.

167
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,559
Find a river.

168
00:14:46,639 --> 00:14:47,559
Weigh it down with stones.

169
00:14:47,919 --> 00:14:48,879
And sink it to the bottom.

170
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,679
What's inside...

171
00:14:51,159 --> 00:14:51,919
Unspeakable.

172
00:15:10,559 --> 00:15:11,519
Let it go.

173
00:15:18,519 --> 00:15:19,759
That's really dangerous.

174
00:15:27,919 --> 00:15:29,000
You mean...

175
00:15:29,919 --> 00:15:32,120
There is someone by your side who shouldn't exist.

176
00:15:32,279 --> 00:15:33,080
Let it go.
